    "text": "The following 1s an algorithm for variable-length packets: 1. Initialize a counter to/n)at the tick of the clock. 2. Ifn is greater than the size of the packet, send the packet and decrement the counter by the packet size. Repeat this step until n is smaller than the packet size. 3. Reset the counter and go to step I. > A leaky bucket algorithm shapes bursty traffic into fixed-rate traffic by averaging the data rate. Drawback: > The leaky bucket algorithm does not credit an idle host. | > For example, if a host is not sending for a while; its bucket becomes empty. Now if the host has bursty data, the leaky bucket allows only an average rate. The time when the host was idle is not taken into account.",
